#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096307 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "97842ba7-b957-51da-9765-18cd94976e5a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12333" :question/problem "Given that\n$\\dfrac{7x+6}{(x+2)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} -\\dfrac{8}{(x+2)^2}$,\n\nwhat is the value of $A$?" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 6 &= A(x + 2) - 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A$.\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-2$, since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x$. So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0$.\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 6 &= A(x + 2) - 8 \\\\\n7(0) + 6 &= A(0 + 2) - 8 \\\\\n6 &= 2A - 8 \\\\\n14 &= 2A \\\\\nA &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096308 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/id #uuid "84d82f4d-b725-5779-a570-cbb3e0e9e429" :question/math-academy-id "e-12334" :question/problem "Given that\n$\\dfrac{7-4x}{(x+5)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+5} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+5)^2}$,\n\nfind the values of $A$ and $B$." :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to solve for $A$ and $B$, and both of these constants appear in the equation simultaneously. However, we can eliminate $A$ if we substitute $x=-5$.\n\nPlugging $x=-5$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + B \\\\\n7 - 4(-5) &= A(-5 + 5) + B \\\\\n27 &= A(0) + B \\\\\n27 &= 0 + B \\\\\n27 &= B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve for $A$. To do this, let’s start by substituting our value $B=27$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A$.\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-5$, since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x$. So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0$.\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + 27 \\\\\n7 - 4(0) &= A(0 + 5) + 27 \\\\\n7 &= 5A + 27 \\\\\n- 20 &= 5A \\\\\nA &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=-4$ and $B=27$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096309 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/id #uuid "57242982-05a3-5104-9bf0-2c6f3350a781" :question/math-academy-id "e-12335" :question/problem "Given that\n$\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+1)}$,\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A\\cdot B\\cdot C$." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the expression through by $(x-3)^2(x+1)$ to give\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^2\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n3(3)^{2} - 5(3) + 8 = B \\cdot 4⟹B = 5\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C$. We get\n\n$$\n3(-1)^{2} - 5(-1) + 8 = C \\cdot (-4)^{2}⟹C = 1\n$$\n\nUnfortunately, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to eliminate both $B$ and $C$. However, using our results for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+5(x+1)+1(x-3)^2\n$$\n\nand we can plug in any value of $x$ to solve for $A$. Let's choose the simplest number to plug in, $x=0$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8 &= A(0 - 3)(0 + 1) + 5(0 + 1) + C(0 - 3)^{2} \\\\\n8 &= -3A + 5 + 9 \\\\\n- 6 &= -3A \\\\\nA &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=2\\cdot 5\\cdot 1=10\n$$\n\nand the partial fraction decomposition is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{2}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{5}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096310 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "17bbb974-0c14-5201-a28a-825f4ea385bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12336" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$\\dfrac{1-2x}{(x+1)(x+2)^3}= \\dfrac{A}{x+1}+\\dfrac{B}{x+2} +\\dfrac{C}{(x+2)^2} + \\dfrac{D}{(x+2)^3}$,\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB + CD$." :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)(x+2)^3$ gives\n\n$$\n1 - 2x = A(x+2)^3 + B(x+1)(x+2)^2 + C(x+1)(x+2) + D(x+1)\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(-2) &= A(-2 + 2)^{3} + B(-2 + 1)(-2 + 2)^{2} + C(-2 + 1)(-2 + 2) + D(-2 + 1) \\\\\n1 + 4 &= -D \\\\\nD &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(-1) &= A(-1 + 2)^{3} + B(-1 + 1)(-1 + 2)^{2} + C(-1 + 1)(-1 + 2) + D(-1 + 1) \\\\\n1 + 2 &= A \\\\\nA &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = 0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(0) &= 3(0 + 2)^{3} + B(0 + 1)(0 + 2)^{2} + C(0 + 1)(0 + 2) + (-5)(0 + 1) \\\\\n1 - 0 &= 24 + 4B + 2C - 5 \\\\\n2C &= -4B - 18 \\\\\nC &= -2B - 9.(1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x = 1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(1) &= A(1 + 2)^{3} + B(1 + 1)(1 + 2)^{2} + C(1 + 1)(1 + 2) + D(1 + 1) \\\\\n1 - 2 &= 81 + 18B + 6C - 10 \\\\\n6C &= -18B - 72 \\\\\nC &= -3B - 12.(2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2B - 9 &= -3B - 12 \\\\\nB &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $C{:}$\n\n$$\nC = -2(-3) - 9 = -3\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB + CD = 3(-3) + (-3)(-5) = 6\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6057d347-e114-5d79-90e8-f96e5e115906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266317} {:answer/id #uuid "569304e4-bcd0-5079-a323-4c6806fa8522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266318} {:answer/id #uuid "87f61b80-5352-5bfb-acad-74e1e28c82f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266319} {:answer/id #uuid "27412ca7-6d8c-551b-b118-50ba6c97d471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266320} {:answer/id #uuid "27c5c222-355d-57d5-af3f-5643dfc0b9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27c5c222-355d-57d5-af3f-5643dfc0b9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266321} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f206e28-2cd6-59fc-9163-1ead81cfce9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266316}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe6bc6b2-502d-58e9-96c1-e7cee67c2b89" :question/math-academy-id "q-10993" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+21}{(x-4)^{2}(3-x)}=\\frac{A}{x-4}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{3-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides by $(x-4)^{2}(3-x)$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-9x+21=A(x-4)(3-x)+B(3-x)+C(x-4)^{2}.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{2}-9(4)+21 & =A(4-4)(3-4)+B(3-4)+C(4-4)^{2} \\\\ 16-36+21 & =B(-1) \\\\ 1 & =-B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}-9(3)+21 & =A(3-4)(3-3)+B(3-3)+C(3-4)^{2} \\\\ 9-27+21 & =C{(-1)}^{2} \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-9(0)+21 & =A(0-4)(3-0)+(-1)(3-0)+3(0-4)^{2} \\\\ 21 & =-12A-3+48 \\\\ 21 & =-12A+45 \\\\ 12A & =24 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 3=-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57e31a9b-dd8b-53f6-8829-afbea9fc1114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x+7}+\\frac{4}{(x+7)^{2}}-\\frac{4}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266324} {:answer/id #uuid "85bd0ae2-c232-59de-ba36-29aff0af88a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x+7}+\\frac{4}{(x+7)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266325} {:answer/id #uuid "4a63cd5f-ec2f-5999-ae66-889ffbc2e1ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{x+7}-\\frac{2}{(x+7)^{2}}-\\frac{4}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266326} {:answer/id #uuid "9a00271a-8db0-593f-9aaa-44d018f3fb7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x+7}-\\frac{2}{(x+7)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266327} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2bd00f-1d2a-598f-b671-3c003919eb3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{x+7}+\\frac{4}{(x+7)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85bd0ae2-c232-59de-ba36-29aff0af88a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x+7}+\\frac{4}{(x+7)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266325} :answer-field/id #uuid "86877b93-522a-516a-89ef-6a418b81c5cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266323}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "562093a1-82de-5994-a12f-6e3f2d1e1558" :question/math-academy-id "q-10995" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-{x}^{2}+20x+149}{(x+7)^{2}(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial     fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}+20x+149}{(x+7)^{2}(x-3)} & =\\frac{A}{x+7}+\\frac{B}{(x+7)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+7)^{2}(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+20x+149=A(x+7)(x-3)+B(x-3)+C(x+7)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor $x=-7$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(-7)^{2}+20(-7)+149 & =A(-7+7)(-7-3)+B(-7-3)+C(-7+7)^{2} \\\\ -49-140+149 & =B(-10) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-40}{-10} \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(3)^{2}+20(3)+149 & =A(3+7)(3-3)+B(3-3)+C(3+7)^{2} \\\\ -9+60+149 & =C{(10)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{200}{100} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({0}^{2})+20(0)+149 & =A(0+7)(0-3)+B(0-3)+C(0+7)^{2} \\\\ 149 & =-21A-3B+49C \\\\ 149 & =-21A-3(4)+49(2) \\\\ 149 & =-21A+86 \\\\ 21A & =-63 \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-{x}^{2}+20x+149}{(x+7)^{2}(x-3)}=-\\frac{3}{x+7}+\\frac{4}{(x+7)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "548a65d2-4d6c-5328-b863-20d25619f8f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266331} {:answer/id #uuid "a1559c3f-0744-54b9-84cb-010ea394d66c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266332} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6a94eb-7c80-5761-afbc-0a9bbc3a32eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266333} {:answer/id #uuid "c14b87f2-ff61-5344-b1bf-43b391f4f048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266334} {:answer/id #uuid "43cdd514-a719-587f-ac8a-a2a020c36d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43cdd514-a719-587f-ac8a-a2a020c36d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266335} :answer-field/id #uuid "77523ba6-ca30-5cf2-a4a7-4e47acc0c839" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266330}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25128f59-a701-583e-8a18-a6f99ce6df78" :question/math-academy-id "q-115101" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-22}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{5}{x-4}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-22 & =5(x-4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(4)-22 & =5(4-4)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97974a7e-ecf8-52b7-8e2f-e1a312bcbe47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266338} {:answer/id #uuid "579d632c-85e8-53b8-a1aa-e46faf4f4b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266339} {:answer/id #uuid "f55eeaf2-8b5b-54c1-8439-4e0bb030b1a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266340} {:answer/id #uuid "70ca6602-ce7f-5840-a978-843e7000c565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266341} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7d6e28-f4ce-5ece-ba66-7cf85d0d57a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ca6602-ce7f-5840-a978-843e7000c565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266341} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1b566a8-075c-5236-bdec-7189dc7b9264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e102b83-78fc-511d-9848-54a531098869" :question/math-academy-id "q-115102" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =1(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & =1(-1+5)+B \\\\ 0 & =4+B \\\\ B & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5911f92e-c722-5dd9-a026-cb757f6663fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266345} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d63ed0-db44-591a-8ec4-95304ca0941e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266346} {:answer/id #uuid "c91fc605-fea6-5b1c-9e21-8a2868061712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266347} {:answer/id #uuid "67db2cdf-4bcf-5ef5-955e-124c956cf029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266348} {:answer/id #uuid "0f7964b5-e1e4-581a-a353-fd990a8f2016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f7964b5-e1e4-581a-a353-fd990a8f2016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266349} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc62e31a-77c8-59cb-8644-112c17bf012c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266344}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f94d7586-f1d9-5b0b-8f86-74d808707b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-115105" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+8}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{5}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+8 & =5(x+2)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)+8 & =5(-2+2)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41551250-7053-5ab8-a51a-f5a1b1c226d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266352} {:answer/id #uuid "e24c90b4-72c1-5f45-8f41-49b8064ae185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266353} {:answer/id #uuid "5a87d9cb-6d60-5b4f-a113-4d0b6f67b391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266354} {:answer/id #uuid "a98ccb93-6c23-5674-a49c-9eac7da199b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266355} {:answer/id #uuid "46690450-110d-5714-a897-ba1c65533cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a98ccb93-6c23-5674-a49c-9eac7da199b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266355} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3faba9-44c2-516c-b9be-83edcb80ec11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266351}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "293e8929-b418-51e0-a83a-fc43f7e0416b" :question/math-academy-id "q-115214" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-6x+9}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+9 & =A(x-2)^{2}+B(x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2}-6(2)+9 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2-2)+C \\\\ 1 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-6(0)+9 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0-2)+1 \\\\ 9 & =4A-2B+1 \\\\ 0 & =4A-2B-8 \\\\ 0 & =2A-B-4 \\\\ B & =2A-4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=1$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2}-6(1)+9 & =A(1-2)^{2}+B(1-2)+1 \\\\ 4 & =A-B+1 \\\\ 0 & =A-B-3 \\\\ B & =A-3.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A-4 & =A-3 \\\\ 2A-A & =-3+4 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =A-3=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =1\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 1=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e0dbd01-f32a-507d-95b3-24e4669d4eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266359} {:answer/id #uuid "46b5afeb-97e3-546e-9836-a517479ec1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266360} {:answer/id #uuid "d484a632-80ce-5061-ab02-ef7c9d2e8ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266361} {:answer/id #uuid "d854b1a7-d75c-563a-8e95-2c76f8c527e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266362} {:answer/id #uuid "5b52f966-e10f-533e-b4db-8a3f4efd5c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d854b1a7-d75c-563a-8e95-2c76f8c527e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266362} :answer-field/id #uuid "cce54225-585f-5c7c-8a6a-837c9b1c837f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266358}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b277ff2-a2f0-5aae-ae88-3cd92c483fac" :question/math-academy-id "q-115238" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+17x+8}{x(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+2}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+2)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB+CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x+2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+17x+8=A(x+2)^{3}+Bx(x+2)^{2}+Cx(x+2)+Dx.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{3}+8(-2)^{2}+17(-2)+8 & =A(-2+2)^{3}+B(-2)(-2+2)^{2}+C(-2)(-2+2)+D(-2) \\\\ -8+32-34+8 & =-2D \\\\ -8+32-34+8 & =-2D \\\\ -2 & =-2D \\\\ D & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{3}+8(0)^{2}+17(0)+8 & =A(0+2)^{3}+B(0)(0+2)^{2}+C(0)(0+2)+D(0) \\\\ 8 & =8A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}+8(-1)^{2}+17(-1)+8 & =1(-1+2)^{3}+B(-1)(-1+2)^{2}+C(-1)(-1+2)+1(-1) \\\\ -1+8-17+8 & =1-B-C-1 \\\\ B & =2-C.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=-3$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{3}+8(-3)^{2}+17(-3)+8 & =1(-3+2)^{3}+B(-3)(-3+2)^{2}+C(-3)(-3+2)+1(-3) \\\\ -27+72-51+8 & =-1-3B+3C-3 \\\\ 3B & =3C-6 \\\\ B & =C-2.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-C & =C-2 \\\\ -2C & =-4 \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $C$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\nB=2-2=0\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB+CD=1(0)+2(1)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e816e0-2e26-5993-8404-1c6d8cd7aa19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266366} {:answer/id #uuid "847c8fa0-b825-5394-9508-44a61d882310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266367} {:answer/id #uuid "6639cb7f-c400-5ba0-a281-84a83db8351d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266368} {:answer/id #uuid "633a86f6-02ee-5ee1-8ecb-8f4e91106009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266369} {:answer/id #uuid "9545dcc6-c087-5a83-93de-2a2f2299a41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "633a86f6-02ee-5ee1-8ecb-8f4e91106009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266369} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d2d005-2859-5bfb-9036-80fb6ce79b8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266365}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ebb07e93-fdbe-5228-b512-65a84db28615" :question/math-academy-id "q-115249" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+1}{(x-1)(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x-2}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x-2)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB-CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)(x-2)^{3}$ to give\n\n$$\n2x+1=A(x-2)^{3}+B(x-1)(x-2)^{2}+C(x-1)(x-2)+D(x-1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+1 & =A(2-2)^{3}+B(2-1)(2-2)^{2}+C(2-1)(2-2)+D(2-1) \\\\ 4+1 & =D \\\\ D & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+1 & =A(1-2)^{3}+B(1-1)(1-2)^{2}+C(1-1)(1-2)+D(1-1) \\\\ 2+1 & =-A \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+1 & =-3(0-2)^{3}+B(0-1)(0-2)^{2}+C(0-1)(0-2)+5(0-1) \\\\ 0+1 & =24-4B+2C-5 \\\\ 2C & =4B-18 \\\\ C & =2B-9.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=3$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)+1 & =-3(3-2)^{3}+B(3-1)(3-2)^{2}+C(3-1)(3-2)+5(3-1) \\\\ 6+1 & =-3+2B+2C+10 \\\\ 2C & =-2B \\\\ C & =-B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2B-9 & =-B \\\\ 3B & =9 \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=-3\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=-3(3)-(-3)(5)=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50b216c3-6c77-5f83-a661-2b960439eb1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266373} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc0f2a4-2113-51e5-b911-2fc4173260db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cc0f2a4-2113-51e5-b911-2fc4173260db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266374} :answer-field/id #uuid "2329c874-ee8f-5c9d-83d4-87658af4418f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5938315a-c866-573c-8a13-1d7be2b6e540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5938315a-c866-573c-8a13-1d7be2b6e540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266376} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a45fa8-41ca-5db1-a38c-aa101b14f9ec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "062ba27e-c67f-5832-95a9-6322bb8e3762" :question/math-academy-id "q-346806" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+2$ |  | $(x+2)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above equality by $(x+2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\nx+3=A(x+2)+B.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3 & =A(-2+2)+B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+3 & =A(0+2)+1 \\\\ 3 & =2A+1 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a7a68d-974d-530e-8135-370d43bfae06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29a7a68d-974d-530e-8135-370d43bfae06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266379} :answer-field/id #uuid "d62fe2c9-529f-578e-bcf1-b7bf26bdf9f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266378}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09ecfa29-3e1d-58ec-bb66-030884bb1735" :question/math-academy-id "q-351180" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{2x+17}{(x+5)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n|  | $\\frac{2x+17}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,=\\,\\frac{2}{(x+5)}\\,\\,+$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $(x+5)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+17}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{(x+5)}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+17 & =2(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-5$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-5)+17 & =2(-5+5)+B \\\\ -10+17 & =0+B \\\\ B & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+17}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{(x+5)}+\\frac{7}{(x+5)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87d7279b-da1a-5d09-855f-675f3e71f350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87d7279b-da1a-5d09-855f-675f3e71f350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266382} :answer-field/id #uuid "075806db-8199-5d17-b07a-535556e86bcb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2cbcf6a-5f35-54d9-b112-d091272783fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2cbcf6a-5f35-54d9-b112-d091272783fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266384} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e03637-c5a8-5d2c-a4ba-a17412de15ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266383}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6baf907-562c-5625-b455-e1c9ae68d5aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-351194" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+1$ |  | $(x+1)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above equality by $(x+1)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n5x-6=A(x+1)+B.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-1)-6 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ B & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-6 & =A(0+1)-11 \\\\ -6 & =A-11 \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1)^{2}}=\\frac{5}{x+1}-\\frac{11}{(x+1)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c6ba72-3c02-5e48-966c-3f177c42697b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266387} {:answer/id #uuid "26bda1d5-c493-576b-a206-2ecdce39aad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60c6ba72-3c02-5e48-966c-3f177c42697b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266387} :answer-field/id #uuid "749b5a75-54b7-5872-a72c-2467985218e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b758cc-a193-5e75-b6f5-cc28c0b9b620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05b758cc-a193-5e75-b6f5-cc28c0b9b620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266390} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2cc9843-e493-50a0-837d-b439dde0257c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266389} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87e9b450-d30b-51e6-8861-866a3f4166b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87e9b450-d30b-51e6-8861-866a3f4166b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266392} :answer-field/id #uuid "685cc6eb-5a6d-57f2-a851-05b8355ff614" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266391}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "15920aaf-9927-5bf8-885c-f575e9e24bf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-351215" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+12}{x(x-2)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+12}{x(x-2)^{2}}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x$ |  | $x-2$ |  | $(x-2)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+12}{x(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-2}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $x(x-2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-18x+12=A(x-2)^{2}+Bx(x-2)+Cx.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-18(0)+12 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0)(0-2)+C(0) \\\\ 12 & =A(-2)^{2} \\\\ 12 & =4A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2)^{2}-18(2)+12 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2)(2-2)+C(2) \\\\ 4 & =C(2) \\\\ 4 & =2C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1)^{2}-18(1)+12 & =3(1-2)^{2}+B(1)(1-2)+2(1) \\\\ 1 & =3(-1)^{2}+B(-1)+2 \\\\ 1 & =3-B+2 \\\\ 1 & =5-B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-18x+12}{x(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{4}{x-2}+\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a65cae1-5c6e-56cc-9836-cb72e5f4217f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a65cae1-5c6e-56cc-9836-cb72e5f4217f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266395} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed94fcdf-a355-5013-94a2-760efd9ef703" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b33aff10-f827-5b37-b3ef-2a4d8ffc7813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b33aff10-f827-5b37-b3ef-2a4d8ffc7813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266397} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f4bb3f2-b5d7-526e-b3d9-24d34b9f34ef" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266396} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c5b8b53-7f15-5985-a809-68ea10b45cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c5b8b53-7f15-5985-a809-68ea10b45cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266399} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfb66f23-f127-5713-90a1-80b89a6eb9e7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266398}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95977e79-a0bc-56f1-b58f-a70a42850ef8" :question/math-academy-id "q-351224" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}\\,=-$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-1$ |  | $2x+3$ |  | $(2x+3)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{2x+3}+\\frac{C}{(2x+3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n-18{x}^{2}-44x-38=A(2x+3)^{2}+B(x-1)(2x+3)+C(x-1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18(1)^{2}-44(1)-38 & =A(2\\cdot 1+3)^{2}+B(1-1)(2\\cdot 1+3)+C(1-1) \\\\ -100 & =A(5)^{2} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-44(-\\frac{3}{2})-38 & =A{(2\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2})+3)}^{2}+B(-\\frac{3}{2}-1)(2\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+C(-\\frac{3}{2}-1) \\\\ -\\frac{25}{2} & =C(-\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18(0)^{2}-44(0)-38 & =A(2\\cdot 0+3)^{2}+B(0-1)(2\\cdot 0+3)+5(0-1) \\\\ -38 & =(-4)(9)+B(-1)(3)-5 \\\\ -38 & =-41-3B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-18{x}^{2}-44x-38}{(x-1)(2x+3)^{2}}=-\\,\\frac{4}{x-1}-\\,\\frac{1}{2x+3}+\\frac{5}{(2x+3)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb4914a0-dcac-553b-a9c1-6e6174cafe91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb4914a0-dcac-553b-a9c1-6e6174cafe91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266402} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba7ad19-e9f0-5861-a329-d1b9a37ee778" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266401} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a23c48-9a8f-566e-b0c3-fec4d39fbacd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75a23c48-9a8f-566e-b0c3-fec4d39fbacd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266404} :answer-field/id #uuid "8394f092-b34a-51bf-a410-97a0251f5a10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d73c11d-74d9-53f9-8208-cc2720a8385c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d73c11d-74d9-53f9-8208-cc2720a8385c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266406} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad10d37-524f-53f8-ba9d-3f87a9a80ee0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266405}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abf4a0bc-708c-5fd0-8c3f-6225acfa1d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-351243" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-2$ |  | $(x-2)^{2}$ |  | $(x-2)^{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-32x+42=A(x-2)^{2}+B(x-2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2)^{2}-32(2)+42 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2-2)+C \\\\ 6 & =C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(3)^{2}-32(3)+42 & =A(3-2)^{2}+B(3-2)+6 \\\\ 9 & =A+B+6 \\\\ B & =3-A.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-32(0)+42 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0-2)+6 \\\\ 42 & =4A-2B+6 \\\\ 36 & =4A-2B \\\\ B & =2A-18.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-A & =2A-18 \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-7 \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{7}{x-2}-\\frac{4}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{6}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b013c49a-7235-534b-95cb-e6ec7aed0156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266409} {:answer/id #uuid "c1337fa2-6a85-5185-841d-9b62fa9933dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266410} {:answer/id #uuid "cebf97f7-73e5-579b-8173-2cc90559fbdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266411} {:answer/id #uuid "2949d997-b7df-5136-ab3e-d8d1234ea639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266412} {:answer/id #uuid "98ec2afa-d2d1-52d4-a6e4-7e098d49502a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ec2afa-d2d1-52d4-a6e4-7e098d49502a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266413} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5d8a44-e752-5b69-8903-594e4b8dff2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266408}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02be96e1-29ee-55e3-9149-ea13abece695" :question/math-academy-id "q-51141" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{(x-1)^{2}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+6=A(x-1)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+6 & =A(-1-1)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1-1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =4C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+6 & =A(1-1)(1+1)+B(1+1)+C(1-1)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =2B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+6 & =A(0-1)(0+1)+4(0+1)+1(0-1)^{2} \\\\ 6 & =-A+4+1 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=(-1)\\cdot 4\\cdot 1=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9e20de9-7934-5d3d-8453-accfc6a1cc4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=1$ and $B=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266416} {:answer/id #uuid "51f742e7-875f-5745-8136-028062c98933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=4$ and $B=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266417} {:answer/id #uuid "5867dc4d-5739-56c8-bfca-904f0a159285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=2$ and $B=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266418} {:answer/id #uuid "836982b5-7b6d-5262-b7ab-25192ad500cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=2$ and $B=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266419} {:answer/id #uuid "7a560135-07d5-5e39-a003-369bbc249dbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=-2$ and $B=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "836982b5-7b6d-5262-b7ab-25192ad500cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=2$ and $B=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266419} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb8ea7a-40a3-5e1f-a328-dde9b745c08b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266415}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e5d3142-b826-521f-9a5c-2fb700156ee4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73189" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+1}{(x+1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{(x+1)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the real constants $A$ and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =A(x+1)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+1 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ -1 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+1 & =A(0+1)-1 \\\\ 2 & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=2$ and $B=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8952609-9bb9-5eb6-8ab6-fb25619a62fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266423} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf8a1ed-587a-5eb2-9520-a17e017f9f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266424} {:answer/id #uuid "c240ea01-468d-585d-8c84-5ba25772ed5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266425} {:answer/id #uuid "ac095963-326c-5723-a1f0-44b90ce7d5bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266426} {:answer/id #uuid "4d464f45-afcf-5eef-8988-eb6d15b06cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d464f45-afcf-5eef-8988-eb6d15b06cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266427} :answer-field/id #uuid "83def415-671f-5880-b321-81e2d42595c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266422}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "077cbb69-7b3a-569b-b9f4-a96c83bfd1a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73195" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-2}{(x+3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+3}-\\frac{17}{(x+3)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2 & =A(x+3)-17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)-2 & =A(0+3)-17 \\\\ -2 & =3A-17 \\\\ 15 & =3A \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb3b040f-6e98-5b4d-be34-06ae9de40bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266430} {:answer/id #uuid "6c656bd2-bed4-539d-912d-51bb0883dbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266431} {:answer/id #uuid "02eb4961-27ed-5a00-9dc8-19b83a986b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266432} {:answer/id #uuid "4326e9e5-891e-5f50-b13e-eb2fd6c927f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266433} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9e7df3-c91b-5412-ad8d-23acff9af924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4326e9e5-891e-5f50-b13e-eb2fd6c927f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266433} :answer-field/id #uuid "95c695ba-88f9-5361-b80e-b43bb442a378" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266429}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c2f7f68-73f1-534c-b6ef-b7e172d22d3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73202" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-6}{(x-9)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-9}+\\frac{B}{(x-9)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-9)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-6 & =A(x-9)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=9$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(9)-6 & =A(9-9)+B \\\\ 21 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)-6 & =A(0-9)+21 \\\\ -6 & =-9A+21 \\\\ 9A & =27 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=3\\cdot 21=63.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0df8ab2-9849-52aa-bebd-ed1f7f12c13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266437} {:answer/id #uuid "282eb657-b6de-5a20-9495-ffb37e01a58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266438} {:answer/id #uuid "d496d1fe-9df7-5aef-84e9-5efa022990aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266439} {:answer/id #uuid "1b294b45-ef42-5446-8f13-3fbe0cde65af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266440} {:answer/id #uuid "642d5ae9-4626-53b4-bc29-de28e517f263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "282eb657-b6de-5a20-9495-ffb37e01a58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266438} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2a334a5-c499-5ea2-9442-3104e07bf9c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266436}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e00e466f-696c-5e44-9bd0-7e09e82c33ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-73377" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+7 & =A(x+4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+7 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+7 & =A(0+4)+3 \\\\ 7 & =4A+3 \\\\ 4 & =4A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=1\\cdot 3=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cf9df0f-763c-555a-a335-1dc78876db06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266444} {:answer/id #uuid "c90ae67a-bc9f-5e88-becf-5ccc3fd0d8de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266445} {:answer/id #uuid "d2197e47-1c94-5019-b985-e3bf921829dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266446} {:answer/id #uuid "1954bb96-9ae7-5fba-867f-c1b6df38dd80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266447} {:answer/id #uuid "33f19410-c93a-5058-aa74-c618d960484b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f19410-c93a-5058-aa74-c618d960484b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266448} :answer-field/id #uuid "772eafbb-edcf-572d-96fc-b5dfcb9333da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266443}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0db90aa3-80f4-55c5-ba22-802ee679163a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73384" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{10-{x}^{2}}{(x-4)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-4}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-4)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-4)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-{x}^{2} & =A(x-4)^{2}+B(x-4)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-{4}^{2} & =A(4-4)^{2}+B(4-4)+C \\\\ -6 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-{0}^{2} & =A(0-4)^{2}+B(0-4)-6 \\\\ 10 & =16A-4B-6 \\\\ 0 & =16A-4B-16 \\\\ 0 & =4A-B-4 \\\\ B & =4A-4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=3$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-{3}^{2} & =A(3-4)^{2}+B(3-4)-6 \\\\ 1 & =A-B-6 \\\\ 0 & =A-B-7 \\\\ B & =A-7.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4A-4 & =A-7 \\\\ 3A & =-3 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-1-7=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =-1\\cdot (-8)\\cdot (-6)=-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
